+note cnt_word: OM-2 `count A off n v`, a ulong: how many of the n uchar elements of A from off equal v.
+note A is an array name (a local, global, text, or a view or edit parameter, sized or unsized); off and n
+note are ulong, v is uchar. The four values are read left to right; then the slice is checked exactly as
+note read and write check theirs (vs_chk: a non-uchar A is error 7; n <= len A and off <= len A - n, else
+note trap 3), and only then is any element read, so an out-of-bounds slice traps 3 whatever v is and an
+note in-bounds one never traps. A tracked fresh array (error 27, fz_arg), a struct or layout (error 7) and
+note a contract clause (error 30, cp_token) are refused; an IR unit is never OM-2, so count is no word there
+note (error 3), and the irmode guard (error 9, as dit) only keeps it so. Code (AArch64): P = A + off
+note (ADD, C6.2.6), M = n (MOV = ORR), V0 = v in all 16 byte lanes (DUP), S = 0 (MOVZ, C6.2.285); then
+note while M >= 16 (CMP, C6.2.96; B.LO, C6.2.34): a block of K = min(M >> 4, 255) chunks (LSR = UBFM,
+note C6.2.487; CMP; B.LS; MOVZ X16, #255; V1 = 0 by MOVI, C7.2.247), each chunk LD1 {V2.16B}, [P], #16
+note (post-index), CMEQ V2, V2, V0 (0xff where equal), SUB V1.16B, V1, V2 (+1 per equal lane; 255 chunks
+note keep each lane <= 255), SUB M, M, #16, SUBS X16, X16, #1, B.NE; then UADDLV H2, V1.16B (the 16 lanes,
+note at most 4080), UMOV W16, V2.H[0], ADD S, S, X16, B back (C6.2.35). The last M < 16 bytes one at a
+note time: CBZ M (C6.2.78), UMOV WK, V0.B[0], LDRB W16, [P], #1 (post-index), CMP W16, WK, CINC S, S, EQ
+note (CSINC), SUBS M, M, #1, B.NE. Every word is a fixed part from the instruction's Arm ARM encoding ORed
+note with register fields; each fixed part was checked against llvm-mc 18 at two or more register
+note choices. P, M, S and K are new temporaries, so no name's register changes; X16 is scratch;
+note V0-V2 carry nothing between operations (see scrub). The result moves to the destination after the
+note temporaries are given back.
+fn cnt_word dst ulong to void
+if ne get irmode 0 0
+fail 9
+end
+x = mul get depth 0 32
+sl = get nslot 0
+put fr add x 8 sl
+e = arrname
+fz_arg e
+if ge get nm_kind sub e 1 6
+fail 7
+end
+rdval 0 5 255 0
+vs_off x
+rdval 0 5 255 0
+if ne get rt 0 5
+fail 7
+end
+put fr add x 12 matreg get rk 0 get rv 0 get rt 0
+rdval 0 2 255 0
+if ne get rt 0 2
+fail 7
+end
+v = matreg get rk 0 get rv 0 get rt 0
+ro = get fr add x 11
+rn = get fr add x 12
+vs_chk e ro rn
+if ne get xtarget 0 0
+xcount e ro rn v
+put nslot 0 sl
+d = destreg dst
+xrr 137 0 2
+xstore 0 d
+vdone 1 d 5
+ret
+end
+s = cnt_a64 e ro rn v
+put nslot 0 sl
+d = destreg dst
+if ne d s
+emit or or 2852127712 d shl s 16
+end
+vdone 1 d 5
+end
+
+note cnt_a64: the AArch64 loop of cnt_word (see there), after vs_chk; gives S, the register of the count
+fn cnt_a64 e ulong ro ulong rn ulong v ulong to ulong
